{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f6796095e6532fd109adcd3e678bf9adc42e6a6f8f2de828d56b65baf0224966","digest":{"component_or_area":"test_overlap_retrieve perf gate","key_entities":["tests/unit/test_overlap_retrieve.py","test_perf","rebar.llm.overlap.retrieve()","line 63-66","50ms budget","6558e2bfa"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","performance gate","wall-clock timing","CI runner contention","single-sample measurement"],"propositions":["test_perf asserts a fixed 50ms wall-clock budget on a single run of rebar.llm.overlap.retrieve() over 300 digests, causing flaky failures under CI runner contention","the function's true cost is ~1.6ms median locally with ~30x margin to budget, but CI samples inflate to 289.5ms (~180x true cost) due to transient runner scheduling contention","single-sample wall-clock measurements are not robust to shared-runner CPU scheduling and do not reflect algorithmic performance","the fix measures minimum elapsed time across N>=5 runs and asserts min < budget to filter transient contention while retaining guardrail teeth for real regressions"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787797594225846001,"uuid":"850f7efc-d4ca-447e-9517-d42e61e088f1"}